Badia Ground Cumin
&#xD;
Cumin has long been a signature spice and is a key ingredient in various spice blends and many beans, couscous, curries, rice and vegetable dishes. It&#xA0;works well in combination with allspice, anise seed, brown mustard, cardamom, cinnamon, coriander, fennel, fenugreek, garlic, ginger, nutmeg, paprika, turmeric and yellow mustard.
&#xD;
Cumin flourishes when used with beans, bread, cabbage, pungent cheeses, chicken, eggplant, lamb, lentils, onions, potatoes, rice, sauerkraut and squash.

Badia Dill Weed
