Since an open box of Baking Soda naturally absorbs unwanted smells and odors, always use a fresh, unopened box of Arm &amp; Hammer Baking Soda to make the best tasting cookies and cakes.
&#xD;
&#xD;
America's #1 Trusted Baking Soda brand&#xD;
Versatile, effective and affordable for over 170 years&#xD;
Use for baking, cleaning, deodorizing and more&#xD;
Free of harsh chemicals and gentle enough to use on many surfaces&#xD;
&#xD;
Delectable Cookie Recipe:
&#xD;
&#xD;
2 1/4 cups unsifted flour&#xD;
1 teaspoon Arm &amp; Hammer Baking Soda&#xD;
1 teaspoon salt&#xD;
1 cup softened butter or margarine&#xD;
3/4 cup granulated sugar&#xD;
3/4 cup brown sugar, packed&#xD;
1 teaspoon vanilla extract&#xD;
2 eggs&#xD;
2 cups (12oz.) semi-sweet chocolate chips&#xD;
1 cup chopped nuts (peanuts, walnuts or pecans)&#xD;
&#xD;
Cooking Instructions:&#xA0;Pre-heat oven to 375&#xB0;F.&#xA0;&#xA0;In a small bowl, sift together flour, baking soda and salt.&#xA0;In a large bowl, combine butter, sugars and vanilla. With a wooden spoon, beat until creamy.&#xA0;Beat in eggs. Gradually add sifted dry ingredients. Mix well. Stir in chocolate chips and nuts. Drop by&#xA0;rounded teaspoonfuls onto ungreased cookie sheets. Bake in 375&#xB0;F oven for 8 minutes or until lightly browned.

