How to Make Melted Snowman Cookies
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1&#xBD; Stick (1/4 Cup) Softened Butter, Margarine, or Spread&#xD;
1 Tablespoon Water&#xD;
&#xD;
Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Heat the oven to 190.56&#xB0;C (or 176.67&#xB0;C for nonstick cookie sheets). Place the fudge pouch in a bowl of hot water (do not microwave the pouch); set aside.&#xD;
Stir the cookie mix, softened butter, and water in a medium bowl until the dough forms. Drop the dough by tablespoonfuls 2 inches apart on an ungreased cookie sheet.&#xD;
Bake for 10 to 12 minutes or until the edges are light golden brown. Cool for 2 minutes before removing from the cookie sheet. Cool completely.&#xD;
Squeeze the marshmallow pouch for 15 seconds to soften (do not microwave the pouch). Cut a 1/4-inch tip from the corner of the marshmallow pouch. Squeeze about 2 teaspoons of marshmallow topping on a cookie to create a melted snowman. Immediately place candy eyes on the marshmallow topping so they stick.&#xD;
Squeeze the fudge pouch for 15 seconds. Cut a 1/4-inch tip from the corner of the fudge pouch. Decorate snowman. Store tightly covered.&#xD;
&#xD;
Note: For high altitudes (3500 to 6500 ft), stir 1 tbsp all-purpose flour into the dry cookie mix.
&#xD;
Warning: Do not eat raw cookie dough.

