How to Make Hot Cocoa
&#xD;
&#xD;
To make a cup of soothing cocoa drink, put one teaspoon of Van Houten Cocoa Powder into a breakfast mug.&#xD;
Fill the mug with boiling water and quickly stir. It is essential that the water should be absolutely boiling.&#xD;
Add skimmed milk powder, low-fat UHT milk, or evaporated milk.&#xD;
Add sugar to your desired taste.&#xD;
To make a cup of the finest invigorating chocolate drink, put two and a half teaspoons of Van Houten Cocoa Powder into a breakfast mug. Follow steps 2, 3, and 4.&#xD;
&#xD;
Other Uses:&#xA0;Suitable for baking and drinking. Can be used for making cocoa drinks (hot and iced), chocolate cakes, muffins, cupcakes, cookies, ice cream, yogurt, or as chocolate powder topping on cappuccino or coffee.
&#xD;
Storage Instructions: After transferring Van Houten Cocoa Powder into a container, keep it tightly closed. Store in a cool, clean, and dry place.

Make your mornings more magical with the Pillsbury Funfetti Unicorn Pancake &amp; Waffle Mix! Just add water, cook the batter on a griddle, and you'll get to enjoy pink pancakes or waffles peppered with colorful rainbow sprinkles for breakfast.
&#xD;
&#xD;
Pink batter with rainbow sprinkles&#xD;
For making pancakes and waffles&#xD;
Just add water and cook on the griddle&#xD;
&#xD;
Pancake Cooking Instructions
&#xD;
&#xD;
Get Ready. Coat a griddle with a little vegetable oil. Heat it over medium-high heat, or turn up your electric griddle to 375&#xB0;F. You know your griddle is ready when the drops of water sizzle and disappear. Your pancakes will stick if the griddle is too cool or brown too quickly if it is too hot.&#xD;
Mix your pancake mix and water in a bowl. Mix it until you get rid of any large lumps. Your batter will be a little on the lumpy side. For pancakes a bite above the rest, let your prepped mix stand for 3 minutes. If you want thicker pancakes, just use a little less water. If thinner pancakes are your thing, use a little more water.&#xD;
Pour. Pour a little less than &#xBC; cup of batter for each pancake onto your hot griddle.&#xD;
Cook'em Up. Allow the pancakes to cook for 1&#xBD; minutes on each side or until they're golden brown. Now you're ready to serve up a short stack! Your pancakes are ready to flip when the bottoms are brown and the bubbles on top begin to pop. Careful, flipping them more than once will give you tougher pancakes.&#xD;
&#xD;
Waffle Cooking Instructions
&#xD;
&#xD;
Heat up your waffle iron.&#xD;
Grab a large bowl and toss in: 2 cups pancake mix, 1&#xBC; cups water, &#xBC; cup vegetable oil, and 1 egg.&#xD;
Stir it up and get rid of any large lumps.&#xD;
Bake them in the hot waffle iron until steaming stops and the waffles are golden brown. Makes 12 (4x4-inch) waffles ready to eat.&#xD;
&#xD;
Warning: Do not eat raw batter. Please cook fully before enjoying.

