Cooking Instructions
&#xD;
&#xD;
Cooktop:&#xD;
&#xD;
&#xD;
In a medium saucepan, bring 1 3/4 cups water and 1 tablespoon olive oil or butter just to a boil.&#xD;
Stir in rice and the contents of the spice pack. Return to a boil.&#xD;
Cover; reduce heat to low. Simmer for 20 to 25 minutes, or until most of the water is absorbed.&#xD;
Fluff the pilaf lightly with a fork before serving.&#xD;
&#xD;
Note: At high altitudes, increase water to 2 3/4 cups and cook time to 33 to 38 minutes.
&#xD;
&#xD;
Microwave:&#xD;
&#xD;
&#xD;
In a round 2-quart microwaveable glass casserole, combine rice, contents of the spice sack, 2 1/4 cups of water, and 1 tablespoon of olive oil or butter.&#xD;
Cover; microwave at HIGH for 18 to 21 minutes, or until most of the water is absorbed. Microwave ovens may vary. Adjust times as needed.&#xD;
Let stand for about 5 minutes or until all water is absorbed.&#xD;
Fluff pilaf lightly with a fork before serving.&#xD;
&#xD;
Note: To make low-fat pilaf, follow package directions but omit olive oil or butter and add additional 3 tablespoons water.
