Easy way to prepare palabok:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Soak 500g Super Q Special Palabok in tap water for 10 minutes.&#xD;
Bol palabok in water for 8 to 10 minutes until tender and turn off the heat.&#xD;
Stir to loosen (don't drain) and leave the palabok in hot water for another 15 to 30 minutes.&#xD;
Drain and transfer palabok on a plate, pour sauce, garnish with toppings and serve with patis and calamansi.&#xD;
&#xD;
Easy way to cook palabok sauce:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1 tbsp cooking oil&#xD;
1 Red onion (chopped)&#xD;
2 Shrimp broth cubes&#xD;
5 cups of water&#xD;
2 tbsp patis (fish sauce)&#xD;
1/2 cup achuete water (3 tbsp achuete soak and squeeze in 1/2 cup of water and strain)&#xD;
1/2 cup flour and 1/2 cup cornstarch (Dissolved in a small amount of water)&#xD;
&#xD;
Procedure:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Saute red onion and shrimp broth cubes in cooking oil&#xD;
Add 5 cups of water&#xD;
Add 2 tbsp of patis&#xD;
Add achuete water slowly to desired color&#xD;
Upon boiling, water heat and pour slowly the dissolved mixture of cornstarch and flour while stirring for 10 minutes or until sauce thickens&#xD;
&#xD;
Easy way to make toppings:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1/4 cup miced garlic (saute in oil until light brown)&#xD;
1/4 kilo shrimp (boil in lightly salted water and removed shell when cooked)&#xD;
3 cups flaked and toasted smoked fish (tinapa)&#xD;
1/4 kilo crushed fried rind of chicken or fish&#xD;
